As for drug store - I find it interesting how similar words mean different things in different languages, creating false friends. Your drug store is etymologically related to the Polish drogeria and the French drogurie. However, a drogeria in Polish and droguerie in French is not a pharmacy (the word for a pharmacy is apteka in Polish). You go to a drogeria to buy cosmetics or cleaning supplies. A chain apteka will often be accompanied by a drogeria, but they remain two seperate kinds of establishment, with the drogeria not stocking any medicine.

