This was like a child of a Tuesday and a Friday, no wonder you found it hard. From experience, I recommend you attempt to solve all the puzzles throughout the week. The late week ones will be impossible, at first, but you'll be surprised how quickly you improve. All it takes is experience - the tricky clues have a certain logic to them, and the more of them you see, the easier it will be to deal with further ones.

The autocheck feature is great for beginners. I used it a lot while solving archived puzzles.

@Andrzej

I completely agree with you on this! I know that the official advice is to work Mondays and then Tuesday...   until you feel comfortable moving to the late weeks, but I did it just like you're describing and I think it served me well. Just had to be okay with using help, like training wheels, such as checking the puzzle, etc and or lack of success in my early days of solving later week puzzles. I think it helped me build up my crossword muscles.

Maybe some people get too frustrated and give it up, which is maybe why they recommend building slowly... Guess it depends on your personality. Whether you want to immediately conquer something, or if you want to gradually build up the skills.

